# Auto commit and push

After finishing a batch of code changes the user asked for (bugfix, feature, polish), always:

1. Commit the relevant files with a concise message matching the repo style
2. Push to `origin` on the current branch so Vercel can deploy

Do this without waiting to be asked, unless the user explicitly says not to commit/push, or the only edits are local secrets / `.env` files.

Follow the existing git safety rules (no force push, no amending others' commits, no skipping hooks).
